IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mt-iit`

-- Montana individual income tax -- the taxpayer's seat. Every question is asked as the individual taxpayer (or, for the
-- elderly credit, the claimant) would ask it, with plain inputs; each calls the core in mt-iit.l4 and restates no rule.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Montana individual income tax -- the taxpayer's questions`

§§ `Residence`

@export Am I a Montana resident for state income tax purposes (15-30-2101(31))?
GIVEN `my domicile is in Montana` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Montana is your domicile, the place you treat as your permanent home and intend to return to
      `I keep a permanent place of abode in Montana` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you keep a permanent home in Montana, even if you are temporarily away from the state
      `I have established a residence elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have established a residence in another state or country
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Montana resident` IF
    `is a Montana resident` `my domicile is in Montana` `I keep a permanent place of abode in Montana` `I have established a residence elsewhere`

@export Must I file a Montana return because I moved into or out of Montana during the year (15-30-2112)?
GIVEN `I became or stopped being a Montana resident during the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you changed from resident to nonresident, or from nonresident to resident, during the tax year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file because I moved into or out of Montana` IF
    `I became or stopped being a Montana resident during the tax year`

§§ `My Montana taxable income and tax`

@export What is my Montana taxable income (federal taxable income adjusted under 15-30-2120)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your federal filing status: married filing jointly or surviving spouse, head of household, single, or married filing separately
      `my federal taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal taxable income (IRC s 63), in US dollars, from your federal return
      `state income taxes I itemized` IS A NUMBER @desc State and local income taxes you deducted as an itemized deduction on your federal return (0 if you took the standard deduction)
      `my federal itemized deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your federal itemized deductions (0 if you took the standard deduction)
      `my federal standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal standard deduction you could have taken (IRC s 63(c))
      `my qualified business income deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The qualified business income deduction (IRC s 199A) you claimed federally
      `my other-state bond interest` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest on bonds of other states, territories or their subdivisions (and exempt-interest dividends from it) not already in federal taxable income
      `my other additions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other addition under 15-30-2120(2)(b)-(h) or (k), for example non-qualified withdrawals from a Montana medical care or first-time home buyer savings account
      `my US bond interest and railroad retirement` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest on US government obligations and railroad retirement benefits included in federal taxable income
      `my active-duty military salary subtraction` IS A NUMBER @desc Active-duty armed forces or national guard salary you may subtract under 15-30-2120(3)(c)
      `people on my return aged 65 or over` IS A NUMBER @desc How many taxpayers on the return (you, and your spouse on a joint return) were 65 or older
      `the age 65 subtraction for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The department's inflation-adjusted figure for the 15-30-2120(3)(g) subtraction for the year (the statute's base is $5,500)
      `my ABLE account contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc What you contributed in the year to Montana ABLE or another state's qualified ABLE program accounts of you, your spouse or your Montana-resident child
      `my other subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other subtraction you are entitled to under 15-30-2120(3)-(5), for example family education savings contributions, military retirement income or the volunteer firefighter subtraction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Montana taxable income` MEANS
    `Montana taxable income` `my filing status`
        (`Federal return figures` WITH
            `federal taxable income`                         IS `my federal taxable income`
            `state income taxes deducted as an itemized deduction` IS `state income taxes I itemized`
            `federal itemized deductions in total`           IS `my federal itemized deductions`
            `federal standard deduction allowable`           IS `my federal standard deduction`
            `qualified business income deduction claimed`    IS `my qualified business income deduction`)
        (`Montana adjustments` WITH
            `interest on other states' and territories' obligations not exempt under federal law` IS `my other-state bond interest`
            `other additions under 15-30-2120(2)`            IS `my other additions`
            `US obligation interest and railroad retirement benefits exempt under federal law` IS `my US bond interest and railroad retirement`
            `armed forces and national guard active-duty salary subtraction` IS `my active-duty military salary subtraction`
            `number of taxpayers on the return aged 65 or over` IS `people on my return aged 65 or over`
            `the age 65 subtraction for the year as indexed by the department` IS `the age 65 subtraction for the year`
            `ABLE account contributions`                     IS `my ABLE account contributions`
            `other subtractions under 15-30-2120(3) to (5)`  IS `my other subtractions`)

@export How much Montana income tax do I owe before credits, for tax year 2026 or later (15-30-2103, 15-30-2104)?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year, for example 2026 (years before 2026 are not covered)
      `my filing status for the rates` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your federal filing status: married filing jointly or surviving spouse, head of household, single, or married filing separately
      `my Montana taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Montana taxable income (federal taxable income with the 15-30-2120 additions and subtractions)
      `my net long-term capital gains` IS A NUMBER @desc Net long-term capital gains (IRC s 1222) included in your Montana taxable income
      `I was a Montana resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Montana resident for the whole tax year
      `my Montana source income` IS A NUMBER @desc If not a full-year resident: your Montana source income (income from Montana sources, plus all income received while a Montana resident)
      `my total income from all sources` IS A NUMBER @desc If not a full-year resident: your total income from all sources
      `the published 4.7% bracket ceiling` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for tax years after 2027: the department's inflation-adjusted top of the 4.7% bracket for your filing status (0 if not known)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Montana tax do I owe before credits` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate schedule for` `the tax year` `my filing status for the rates` `the published 4.7% bracket ceiling`
    WHEN `not covered` why THEN `not covered` why
    WHEN `answered` schedule THEN
        `answered`
            (IF `I was a Montana resident all year`
             THEN full
             ELSE `the nonresident tax` full `my Montana source income` `my total income from all sources`)
        WHERE
            full MEANS `the resident tax on` `my Montana taxable income` `my net long-term capital gains` schedule

§§ `Credits`

@export How much is my Montana earned income tax credit (15-30-2318)? It is refundable.
GIVEN `I am a Montana resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Montana resident taxpayer
      `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal earned income credit (IRC s 32) you are eligible for this tax year
      `my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The earned income used to work out your federal earned income credit
      `my earned income from a 501(d) organization` IS A NUMBER @desc Any part of that earned income treated as a dividend from an agricultural organization under IRC s 501(d) (usually 0)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my Montana earned income tax credit` MEANS
    `the Montana earned income tax credit` `I am a Montana resident` `my federal earned income credit` `my earned income` `my earned income from a 501(d) organization`

-- This group only arises for a person aged 62 or over who owns or rents a home in Montana.
§§ `The elderly homeowner and renter credit (only if you are 62 or over)`

@export Am I eligible for Montana's residential property tax credit for the elderly (15-30-2338)?
GIVEN `I was 62 or older during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reached age 62 or older during the year you are claiming for
      `months I lived in Montana` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of the year you resided in Montana
      `months I owned or rented a Montana home` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of the year you lived in one or more Montana dwellings as owner, renter or lessee
      `my gross household income` IS A NUMBER @desc All income of everyone in your household for the year (federal AGI without losses, plus nontaxable income such as Social Security, pensions and public assistance)
      `someone else in my household claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another member of your household is claiming this credit for the same year
      `the department found I took title mainly for the credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department has found that you received title to your home primarily to get this credit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the elderly credit` IF
    `is eligible for the elderly credit` (`the elderly claim from` `I was 62 or older during the year` `months I lived in Montana` `months I owned or rented a Montana home` `my gross household income` 0 0 TRUE `someone else in my household claims` `the department found I took title mainly for the credit`)

@export How much is my Montana residential property tax credit for the elderly (15-30-2340)? It is refundable.
GIVEN `I was 62 or older in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reached age 62 or older during the year you are claiming for
      `months I resided in Montana` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of the year you resided in Montana
      `months I occupied a Montana home` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of the year you lived in one or more Montana dwellings as owner, renter or lessee
      `gross household income` IS A NUMBER @desc All income of everyone in your household for the year (federal AGI without losses, plus nontaxable income such as Social Security, pensions and public assistance)
      `property tax billed on my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Property taxes, special assessments and fees billed on the home you own (up to 1 acre), without penalties or interest, and without any part paid by a public tax subsidy program
      `rent I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Rent you actually paid for the home you rent, in an arm's-length deal, without any part paid by a public rent subsidy program
      `my rented home pays Montana property tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home you rent is subject to Montana property tax, or is rented from a county or municipal housing authority
      `another household member claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another member of your household is claiming this credit for the same year
      `the department found title was taken for the credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department has found that you received title to your home primarily to get this credit
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my elderly credit` MEANS
    `the elderly credit` (`the elderly claim from` `I was 62 or older in the year` `months I resided in Montana` `months I occupied a Montana home` `gross household income` `property tax billed on my home` `rent I paid` `my rented home pays Montana property tax` `another household member claims` `the department found title was taken for the credit`)

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Elderly claim`
`the elderly claim from` a b c d e f g h i MEANS
    `Elderly claim` WITH
        `reached 62 or older during the claim period`      IS a
        `months resided in Montana in the period`          IS b
        `months occupied a Montana dwelling as owner, renter or lessee` IS c
        `gross household income`                           IS d
        `property tax billed on the owned homestead`       IS e
        `gross rent paid for the rented homestead`         IS f
        `the rented dwelling is subject to Montana property tax or rented from a housing authority` IS g
        `another member of the household claims for the period` IS h
        `the department finds title was received primarily to get the credit` IS i

@export By when must I submit my claim for the elderly homeowner or renter credit (15-30-2339(1))?
GIVEN `I must file a Montana income tax return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to file a Montana individual income tax return for the year
      `my return is due on` IS A DATE @desc The day your Montana return is due (if you must file one)
      `the year I am claiming for` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar or tax year you are claiming the credit for
      `April 15 is deferred to` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If April 15 of the next year is an IRS-recognised holiday not observed in Montana, the first business day after it; otherwise nothing
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I claim the elderly credit` MEANS
    `the last day for the elderly credit claim` `I must file a Montana income tax return` `my return is due on` `the year I am claiming for` `April 15 is deferred to`

@export If I missed it, until when may I revise my return and claim the elderly credit (15-30-2339(5))?
GIVEN `the last day I could have claimed` IS A DATE @desc The last day prescribed for filing the claim (your return due date, or April 15 of the following year)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when may I revise and claim the elderly credit` MEANS
    `the last day to revise and claim` `the last day I could have claimed`

§§ `The bottom line`

@export What do I owe Montana, or get back, after the refundable credits (negative means a refund)?
GIVEN `my tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year, for example 2026 (years before 2026 are not covered)
      `my status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your federal filing status: married filing jointly or surviving spouse, head of household, single, or married filing separately
      `my Montana taxable income figure` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Montana taxable income
      `my long-term capital gains` IS A NUMBER @desc Net long-term capital gains included in your Montana taxable income
      `resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Montana resident for the whole tax year
      `Montana source income` IS A NUMBER @desc If not a full-year resident: your Montana source income
      `income from all sources` IS A NUMBER @desc If not a full-year resident: your total income from all sources
      `published bracket ceiling` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for tax years after 2027: the department's inflation-adjusted top of the 4.7% bracket (0 if not known)
      `my Montana earned income tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Montana earned income tax credit (from the earned income tax credit question)
      `my elderly homeowner or renter credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your residential property tax credit for the elderly (from that question; 0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What do I owe Montana after refundable credits` MEANS
    CONSIDER `How much Montana tax do I owe before credits` `my tax year` `my status` `my Montana taxable income figure` `my long-term capital gains` `resident all year` `Montana source income` `income from all sources` `published bracket ceiling`
    WHEN `not covered` why THEN `not covered` why
    WHEN `answered` tax THEN `answered` ((tax MINUS `my Montana earned income tax credit`) MINUS `my elderly homeowner or renter credit`)
